Right now the game listens for **keyboard arrow keys**, so on an iPad we need to add **touch buttons**.

In your CodePen HTML box, find this part:

```html
<p>Use the left and right arrow keys to move the cat.</p>
<canvas id="game" width="500" height="400"></canvas>
```

Replace it with this:

```html
<p>Use the buttons to move the cat.</p>

<button id="leftButton" style="font-size:30px;">⬅️</button>
<button id="rightButton" style="font-size:30px;">➡️</button>

<br>

<canvas id="game" width="500" height="400"></canvas>
```

Then find this part in the code:

```js
document.addEventListener("keyup", function(event) {
  if (event.key === "ArrowLeft") leftPressed = false;
  if (event.key === "ArrowRight") rightPressed = false;
});
```

Right after it, paste this:

```js
const leftButton = document.getElementById("leftButton");
const rightButton = document.getElementById("rightButton");

leftButton.addEventListener("touchstart", function() {
  leftPressed = true;
});

leftButton.addEventListener("touchend", function() {
  leftPressed = false;
});

rightButton.addEventListener("touchstart", function() {
  rightPressed = true;
});

rightButton.addEventListener("touchend", function() {
  rightPressed = false;
});
```

Now you should be able to hold the left and right buttons on your iPad.

